rows.ts_value:
Guarantors are:
- the Borrowers and the existing guarantors;
- future material subsidiaries organised in Eligible Jurisdictions (the jurisdictions of existing Guarantors), with materiality thresholds consistent with the Existing CA;
- any subsidiary Capri elects to make a guarantor.

Exceptions are to be agreed and include legal prohibition or required consents, non-wholly-owned subsidiaries barred by their organisational documents, and non-ECP subsidiaries for swaps. A CFC or CFC Holding Company, other than an IP Subsidiary, does not guarantee domestic obligations. The Administrative Agent can exclude a subsidiary on cost-benefit grounds.

The guarantee covers the RCF, hedging with Lenders (those who were Lenders on the Closing Date for existing swaps, or when a new swap is entered into), Supply Chain Financings that are not excluded, Bilateral Letters of Credit and existing Working Capital Facilities.

Proceeds will be used:
(i) on the Closing Date, to repay in part the revolving loans outstanding under the Existing Credit Agreement;
(ii) to pay costs and expenses of the amendment, the RCF and the use of proceeds;
(iii) for general corporate purposes of the Loan Parties and their Subsidiaries.

rows.ca_value:
Revolving Loan proceeds may be used only:
(i) on the Amendment No. 1 Effective Date, to repay the Existing Revolving Loans (blackline replaces 'Term' with 'Revolving');
(ii) to pay fees, costs and expenses of Capri Holdings and its Subsidiaries in connection with Amendment No. 1;
(iii) for working capital, capex, Permitted Acquisitions, permitted Investments, Restricted Payments 'permitted under Section 6.06', and other general corporate purposes of Capri Holdings and its Subsidiaries.

The usual margin stock and sanctions/anti-corruption restrictions also apply.

rows.ts_value:
Substantially as in the Existing CA and to include:
- non-payment of principal when due;
- non-payment of interest, fees or other amounts after a 5 business day grace period;
- material misrepresentation;
- covenant breach (with grace periods for certain affirmative covenants);
- documents ceasing to be in effect;
- cross-default;
- bankruptcy;
- material judgments;
- ERISA events;
- change of control;
- material provisions becoming invalid;
- foreign-law events.
No dollar thresholds are stated.

rows.ca_value:
Article VII:
(a) principal or LC reimbursement when due;
(b) interest, fees or other amounts, with a 5 Business Day grace period;
(c) misrepresentation in any material respect;
(d) immediate default for breach of 5.02(a), 5.03 (existence), 5.08, 5.09 or Article VI;
(e) other covenants, 30 days after notice;
(f)-(g) payment default on, or acceleration of, Material Indebtedness above $50m;
(h)-(j) insolvency, with involuntary cases undismissed for 60 days;
(k) judgments above $50m (not paid or insured) undischarged for 60 consecutive days, or attachment;
(l) ERISA events causing a MAE;
(m) Change in Control;
(n) Loan Document invalidity;
(o)-(q) BVI, Swiss and UK insolvency events;
(r) loss of perfection over a material portion of the Collateral.

Change in Control means any of:
(a) a person or group acquiring more than 35% of the voting power of Capri Holdings;
(b) a majority of Capri Holdings' board made up of non-continuing directors;
(c) Capri Holdings ceasing to own and Control 100% of any other Borrower (excluding directors' qualifying shares and nominal shares for foreign nationals).
It is an Event of Default under Article VII(m).

rows.ts_value:
Assignments to eligible assignees need consent (not to be unreasonably withheld) of:
- MK, which is deemed to consent after 10 business days, and whose consent is not needed for assignments to Lenders, affiliates or approved funds, or during a payment or bankruptcy event of default;
- the Administrative Agent;
- each Issuing Bank and the Swingline Lender.

Minimum assignment: $5,000,000 unless MK and the Administrative Agent agree otherwise. Participations are as in the Existing CA, with no greater yield-protection payments and votes limited to matters needing each affected Lender. Pledges are permitted without release of the Lender.

rows.ca_value:
Permitted Equivalent Indebtedness is secured or unsecured debt of Capri Holdings or a Loan Party, subject to:
(i) no Default or Event of Default before or after incurrence;
(ii) no guarantee by a subsidiary that is not a Loan Party;
(iii) if secured, only on the Collateral, pari passu or junior, under an intercreditor agreement in the form of Exhibit K-1 or K-2;
(iv) covenants no more restrictive than market terms, as determined in good faith by Capri Holdings;
(v) no maturity or scheduled amortization before 91 days after the latest Maturity Date.
The Ratio Incremental Amount allows unsecured debt at Net Leverage Ratio of 4.00x or less and secured debt at Secured Net Leverage Ratio of 3.00x or less. The Secured Net Leverage Ratio is amended to use Consolidated EBITDA instead of Consolidated EBITDAR as its denominator. Permitted under s.6.01(u), with liens under s.6.02(s).

Section 2.27: the Company may, by written notice of at least 5 Business Days, establish Replacement Revolving Facilities or Replacement Term Facilities. Conditions:
- no Default or Event of Default;
- representations true;
- maturity no earlier than the replaced facility and no amortization;
- amount capped at the replaced amount plus fees and costs;
- pari passu, with the same Guarantors, secured only by the Collateral;
- terms no more favourable than the replaced facility.
Under s.9.02(c)(iii), the Company and the Administrative Agent may amend the agreement to implement it. Amendment No. 1 was itself done under s.2.27.
